notes:
Retaken in Unity 7000.0.0a20 (trunk build of 2026-11-17) at the original's scale (Scene view 800x504pt with the menu at 2x, as in the original), with the same rebuilt model and camera angle as #10 and the main block selected (orange outline). The right-click menu is a native Windows menu that Unity's capture can't see. Since trunk PR #137579 ('Owner-draw Windows editor menus in the editor skin colors') Unity paints these menus itself, so the menu is drawn to that code (Editor/Platform/Windows/MenuThemeWin.cpp):
- background: --unity-colors-app_toolbar-background (20,20,20);
- text: --unity-colors-default-text (210,210,210);
- disabled text and the 1px border/separators: blended from those, per the code;
- metrics: Segoe UI 9pt, 22px rows, 32px gutter, Unity's own submenu chevron, small rounded corners.
Every item, separator, shortcut and enabled state comes from Unity 7 itself (GameObjectToolContext.PopulateMenu, re-dumped on the new build; unchanged). Unity 7 menu changes vs the original: 'Move to Grid Position' is now 'Move to Closest Grid Point' plus 'Align to Grid Rotation', there's a new 'Grid' submenu, and there's no 'Prefab' submenu here. Shown without a hover highlight, since no pointer is drawn (the hover colour would be --unity-colors-app_toolbar_button-background-hover, 60,60,60).

Retaken in Unity 7000.0.0a20 (trunk build of 2026-11-17) at the original's scale (Scene view 800x504pt with the menu at 2x, as in the original), with the same rebuilt model and camera angle as #10 and the main block selected (orange outline). The right-click menu is a native Windows menu that Unity's capture can't see. Since trunk PR #137579 ('Owner-draw Windows editor menus in the editor skin colors') Unity paints these menus itself, so the menu is drawn to that code (Editor/Platform/Windows/MenuThemeWin.cpp):
- background: --unity-colors-app_toolbar-background (20,20,20);
- text: --unity-colors-default-text (210,210,210);
- disabled text and the 1px border/separators: blended from those, per the code;
- metrics: Segoe UI 9pt, 22px rows, 32px gutter, Unity's own submenu chevron, small rounded corners.
Every item, separator, shortcut and enabled state comes from Unity 7 itself (GameObjectToolContext.PopulateMenu, re-dumped on the new build; unchanged). Unity 7 menu changes vs the original: 'Move to Grid Position' is now 'Move to Closest Grid Point' plus 'Align to Grid Rotation', there's a new 'Grid' submenu, and there's no 'Prefab' submenu here. Shown without a hover highlight, since no pointer is drawn (the hover colour would be --unity-colors-app_toolbar_button-background-hover, 60,60,60).

Rebuilt for Unity 7000.0.0a20 (trunk build of 2026-11-17) at 2120x1280 (about 2.2px/pt), in the original's arrangement, from real Unity 7 pieces on Atrio:
- the main toolbar (left group, Play/Pause/Step and right group, grabbed from its own buffer);
- a Scene view with the Default overlay preset over an aerial view of the courtyard;
- an Inspector on Atrio's Camera (Camera > Projection open);
- a floating Hierarchy expanded to the camera (Atrio > Gameplay > Player > FirstPerson);
- the Project window's folder pane at the original's 273pt width (Favorites collapsed; Assets > EFDS_Screenshots > GameplaySequenceDemo > Info expanded). Unity keeps 55pt for the asset list, so the window's real tab and toolbar come from a 273pt window and the tree from the folder pane of a wider window set to exactly 273pt; both are unedited Editor pixels.
The Scene pane menu is drawn to Unity's owner-draw code from the real items HostView.PopupGenericMenu builds. Annotations:
- indentation callouts in the original's style (shaded base strip with a bracket under the window, a dashed guide per indent level, bars on rows without foldout arrows), with values read live from the folder tree (GetContentIndent): base strip 20px (2pt base indent + 18pt foldout; the original said 15px) and 14px per level (indentWidth; the original said 15px). Bars are on levels 1, 3 and 4 (_Recovery, Animation, Icons): no visible level-2 row lacks a foldout arrow in this project, so the original's fourth bar is omitted.
- the token chip shows the live value of --unity-colors-label-text-focus in Unity 7, #A4CEEB (the original showed #81B4FF).
Not reproduced: the original's UI Builder Slider tile and selected-element callout (UI Builder's viewport and selection couldn't be driven reliably from code), and the focused 'Clipping Planes' label (the URP Camera inspector is IMGUI, so its focus state can't be set without input); the token chip stands on its own. PRIVACY: the toolbar's account button shows the capturing user's initials.

